{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "L"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 139, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Restoring the direct input-to-output residual when it is missing yields large gains (exps 22, 26, 28) versus small or negative effects when it replaces a conv or pool."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty edge 3 with a 1x1 conv adds a missing direct path and helps strongly (exps 92, 94, 96, 98), unlike replacing an existing skip or conv."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting the input-to-output skip removes the cell's residual connection and causes especially severe drops (exps 6, 7)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a harmful avg-pool on the last edge into the output with a 3x3 conv gives the largest gains (exps 18, 20)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "When the parent already has a 3x3 conv into the output, adding another on edge 5 brings little or negative benefit (exps 11-15) compared with weaker parents (exps 16-20)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing parameter-free avg-pool on the first edge with a 3x3 conv gives large gains (exps 33, 37) versus near-zero or negative gains from other ops."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing a harmful avg-pool on edge 0 improves accuracy (exp 83), while removing a skip or conv there tends to hurt."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": 